  "        ""section"": ""A product of units is ± the unit at the XOR of their indices"","
  "        ""text"": ""dimension ${n}: e${a} e${b} = ±e${a ^ b}"""
  "      },"
  "      {"
  "        ""section"": ""So the tripods are the lines of PG(n-1, 2): (2^n - 1)(2^n - 2)/6"","
  "        ""text"": ""octonions 7, sedenions 35, trigintaduonions 155, 64-ions 651"""
  "      },"
  "      {"
  "        ""section"": ""So the tripods are the lines of PG(n-1, 2): (2^n - 1)(2^n - 2)/6"","
  "        ""text"": ""the 64-ions have 63 imaginary units: the 6-bit closure"""
  "      },"
  "      {"
  "        ""section"": ""Wikipedia's 155, as listed"","
  "        ""text"": ""the listed 155 are exactly the lines of PG(4, 2)"""
  "      },"
  "      {"
  "        ""section"": ""Wikipedia's 155, as listed"","
  "        ""text"": ""e${a} e${b} = ±e${c} in the trigintaduonions"""
